NO LOCAL PATCHES. Everything Caravel needs is in the upstream source.

This build adds exact fees before signing (fees-exact):
  - browser-writer.ts : prepareRegisterWithNostr(name, npub, budgetFor?) → PreparedOnsWrite. The fee
                        input is chosen ONCE, dry-run to learn the cost, and the REAL transaction is
                        built and sealed at the caller's budget; submit() sends that envelope, once
                        (no rescan, reselection or rebuild). simulate() dry-runs a twin at the same
                        fee and accepts only when total_fees_required is within it — the dry run
                        itself does not enforce the fee. The estimate reads total_fees_required
                        first. submitRegisterWithNostr and the single-call writes go through prepare.
  - index.ts          : exports the PreparedOnsWrite type.
  - tests             : npm test — 14, unchanged (node:test via tsx); excluded from this dist.

Carried forward from the 0.43 build (Ootle 0.43 / @tari-project/ootle 0.7, ootle-wasm 0.43):
  - retry.ts          : NEW. Busy-indexer retry (0.43 rate limits: 429, dry-run cap: 503).
                        Reads and dry runs retry with Retry-After / jittered backoff; a submit is
                        retried only on a busy refusal, only with the same sealed envelope, and
                        only after the fee input is confirmed unspent. Ambiguous failures are
                        never resubmitted. IndexerBusyError / SubmitMaybeLandedError and the
                        NETWORK_BUSY_MESSAGE / RETRYING_MESSAGE strings are exported.
  - reader.ts         : registry read retries.
  - browser-writer.ts : UTXO scan, result poll, dry run, epoch + input resolution retry; submit via
                        submitOnce. BrowserSigner.onProgress (optional) carries the busy notice.
  - package.json      : peer deps @tari-project/ootle* ^0.7.0, ootle-wasm ^0.43.0. The 0.7 SDK
                        dist is byte-identical to 0.6, so no API change was needed.
